  {
   "id": "mlsqMLQKU64J",
   "from": "Benjamin Birnbaum",
   "author": "7f07abeab4f11b50",
   "date": "2015-05-01T00:20:08Z",
   "subject": "Re: Trouble with rJava and packrat",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks for the quick reply!  After running<div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">sudo R CMD javareconf</font></div><div><br></div><div>packrat::restore() worked, but I had to first uninstall java and reinstall it with</div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">sudo apt-get install openjdk-7-*</font><br></div><div><br></div><div>(Other methods of java installation caused sudo R CMD javareconf to fail.)</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m still confused about why the workaround didn&#39;t work -- in particular why <span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">/usr/lib/R/site-library/ </span>disappeared from libPaths() when I ran in packrat mode.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Thursday, April 30, 2015 at 6:15:19 PM UTC-4, Kevin Ushey wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Hi Benjamin,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">One thing worth trying — can you install <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">rJava</code> manually from within R, e.g. with:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,255)\">install.packages(&quot;rJava&quot;)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">You may also need to run</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,255)\">sudo R CMD javareconf\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">after installing and updating Java, to ensure R is properly detecting the current available Java toolset.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Let me know if that helps!<br>Kevin</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">On Thursday, April 30, 2015 at 2:42:14 PM UTC-7, Benjamin Birnbaum wrote:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\"></p><div><p></p><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;m trying to use Packrat for reproducible package management across Mac laptops and Ubuntu machines, and I&#39;m having trouble with with the rJava package.<div><br></div><div>What I did:</div><div>- On the Mac, I navigated into an existing R project, opened the R CLI, and ran packrat::init(). There were no errors.</div><div>- I copied the R code and &quot;packrat/packrat.lock&quot; &quot;packrat/packrat.opts&quot; &quot;packrat/src/&quot; to the Ubuntu machine</div><div>- On the Ubuntu machine, I navigated into the R project directory, and started the R CLI</div><div><br></div><div>This fails with the following output:</div><div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">The command failed with output:</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">* installing *source* package &#39;rJava&#39; ...</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">** package &#39;rJava&#39; successfully unpacked and MD5 sums checked</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking for gcc... gcc -std=gnu99</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking whether the C compiler works... yes</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking for C compiler default output file name... a.out</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking for suffix of executables...</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking whether we are cross compiling... no</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking for suffix of object files... o</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking whether we are using the GNU C compiler... yes</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking whether gcc -std=gnu99 accepts -g... yes</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking for gcc -std=gnu99 option to accept ISO C89... none needed</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking how to run the C preprocessor... gcc -std=gnu99 -E</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking for grep that handles long lines and -e... /bin/grep</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking for egrep... /bin/grep -E</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking for ANSI C header files... yes</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking for sys/wait.h that is POSIX.1 compatible... yes</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking for sys/types.h... yes</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking for sys/stat.h... yes</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking for stdlib.h... yes</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking for string.h... yes</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">checking for memory.h.</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">In addition: Warning message:</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">In restore(restart = FALSE) :</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  The most recent snapshot was generated using R version 3.1.3</font></div></div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve ensured that java is installed on the Ubuntu machine.</div><div><br></div><div>As a workaround, I also explored installing rJava directly via <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">sudo apt-get install r-cran-rjava</font> and then setting it as an external library.</div><div><br></div><div>I can successfully run <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">library(&#39;rjava&#39;)</font> outside of the packrat project.  But when I try to add it as an external library inside of the packrat project, I see</div><div><br></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">&gt; packrat::set_opts(external.packages = c(&quot;rJava&quot;))</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Error in results[sapply(results, Negate(isTRUE))] :</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  invalid subscript type &#39;list&#39;</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">In addition: Warning message:</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">In symlinkExternalPackages(project = project) :</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  The following external packages could not be located:</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">- &#39;rJava</font></div></div><div><br></div><div>Further investigation reveals that rJava is installed under <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">/usr/lib/R/site-library/rJava</font> but when I look at the libPaths in the packrat project, the site-library directory isn&#39;t there:</div><div><br></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">&gt; .libPaths()</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">[1] &quot;/srv/encrypted_fs/flatiron/code/bbirnbaum_r_packages/repo/blocks/blocks/pharma/analytics/research/Amgen_QA/packrat/lib/x86_64-pc-linux-gnu/3.2.0&quot;</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">[2] &quot;/srv/encrypted_fs/flatiron/code/bbirnbaum_r_packages/repo/blocks/blocks/pharma/analytics/research/Amgen_QA/packrat/lib-ext&quot;</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">[3] &quot;/usr/lib/R/library&quot;</font></div></div><div><br></div><div>What can I do to make rJava work?  Ideally, it would just work without the external package workaround, but even getting that to work would be ok.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks!</div><div><br></div></div></blockquote><p></p></div><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\"></p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:SGkgQmVuamFtaW4sPGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj5PbmUgdGhpbmcgd29ydGggdHJ5aW5nIC0t\r\nIGNhbiB5b3UgaW5zdGFsbCBgckphdmFgIG1hbnVhbGx5IGZyb20gUiwgZS5nLiB3aXRoOjwvZGl2\r\nPjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+Jm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyBpbnN0YWxsLnBhY2thZ2VzKCJySmF2\r\nYSIpPC9kaXY+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj4/IFlvdSBtYXkgYWxzbyBuZWVkIHRvIHJ1bjwv\r\nZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+Jm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyBzdWRvIFIgQ01EIGphdmFyZWNv\r\nbmY8L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2PmFmdGVyIGluc3RhbGxpbmcgYW5kIHVwZGF0aW5n\r\nIEphdmEsIHRvIGVuc3VyZSBSIGlzIHByb3Blcmx5IGRldGVjdGluZyB0aGUgY3VycmVudCBhdmFp\r\nbGFibGUgSmF2YSB0b29sc2V0LjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+VGhhbmtzLDwvZGl2\r\nPjxkaXY+S2V2aW48L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj5PbiBUaHVyc2RheSwgQXByaWwgMzAsIDIwMTUgYXQg\r\nMjo0MjoxNCBQTSBVVEMtNywgQmVuamFtaW4gQmlybmJhdW0gd3JvdGU6PGJsb2NrcXVvdGUgY2xh\r\nc3M9ImdtYWlsX3F1b3RlIiBzdHlsZT0ibWFyZ2luOiAwO21hcmdpbi1sZWZ0OiAwLjhleDtib3Jk\r\nZXItbGVmdDogMXB4ICNjY2Mgc29saWQ7cGFkZGluZy1sZWZ0OiAxZXg7Ij48ZGl2IGRpcj0ibHRy\r\nIj5JJ20gdHJ5aW5nIHRvIHVzZSBQYWNrcmF0IGZvciByZXByb2R1Y2libGUgcGFja2FnZSBtYW5h\r\nZ2VtZW50IGFjcm9zcyBNYWMgbGFwdG9wcyBhbmQgVWJ1bnR1IG1hY2hpbmVzLCBhbmQgSSdtIGhh\r\ndmluZyB0cm91YmxlIHdpdGggd2l0aCB0aGUgckphdmEgcGFja2FnZS48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48\r\nZGl2PldoYXQgSSBkaWQ6PC9kaXY+PGRpdj4tIE9uIHRoZSBNYWMsIEkgbmF2aWdhdGVkIGludG8g\r\nYW4gZXhpc3RpbmcgUiBwcm9qZWN0LCBvcGVuZWQgdGhlIFIgQ0xJLCBhbmQgcmFuIHBhY2tyYXQ6\r\nOmluaXQoKS4gVGhlcmUgd2VyZSBubyBlcnJvcnMuPC9kaXY+PGRpdj4tIEkgY29waWVkIHRoZSBS\r\nIGNvZGUgYW5kICJwYWNrcmF0L3BhY2tyYXQubG9jayIgInBhY2tyYXQvcGFja3JhdC5vcHRzIiAi\r\ncGFja3JhdC9zcmMvIiB0byB0aGUgVWJ1bnR1IG1hY2hpbmU8L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pi0gT24gdGhlIFVi\r\ndW50dSBtYWNoaW5lLCBJIG5hdmlnYXRlZCBpbnRvIHRoZSBSIHByb2plY3QgZGlyZWN0b3J5LCBh\r\nbmQgc3RhcnRlZCB0aGUgUiBDTEk8L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2PlRoaXMgZmFpbHMg\r\nd2l0aCB0aGUgZm9sbG93aW5nIG91dHB1dDo8L2Rpdj48ZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+\r\nPGZvbnQgZmFjZT0iY291cmllciBuZXcsIG1vbm9zcGFjZSI+VGhl